  recipeId: led
  concept: "Authored objective: Automatic isolated transfer.\nAuthored requirement:
    MAIN is open; backup diode powers LED while main/charge/source current stays
    below 0.10 mA. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required.\nGeneral teaching principle:
    An LED has a defined anode and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current
    control matter for normal forward operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game
    evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Automatic isolated transfer\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Automatic isolated transfer\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 29, perform the objective \u2018Automatic isolated transfer\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: MAIN is open;
    backup diode powers LED while main/charge/source current stays below 0.10 mA.
    current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion;
